This component continues the same applicant's Poincare formalization work.

The basepoint-independence helper was copied from the existing checked
Poincare-Conjecture implementation at
d5cf293fcee9164a449fcc833d049d51aab52bc3, under Apache License 2.0.
An earlier unpublished cap-filling candidate by the same applicant supplied
the quotient, Tietze and loop-generation starting code. The candidate was
not a completed or publicly accepted theorem; its new extension, fixes and
verification are documented in this component.

HatcherLib is the separately authored reference library pinned at
bb91a091f0b968f8bbe8d861e025a88d82b161be, in
https://github.com/frenzymath/Poincare-Conjecture/tree/bb91a091f0b968f8bbe8d861e025a88d82b161be/formalized-sources/Hatcher
The component uses its proved van Kampen surjectivity and circle group
calculation, not a missing kernel-identification theorem. Those authors,
Hatcher, Lean and Mathlib retain the relevant mathematical and code credit.

Local Lean and Python code is under the included Apache License 2.0.
Dependencies and build caches are not redistributed. This research component
is not an eligible complete-original-problem prize submission and makes no
formalization-priority, solver-credit, allocation or payment claim.
